### Topic 52 - Scheduling, Async and Events
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension. WATCH THE APPLICATION LOG while sending!

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1) Register a user -> 201 in a few ms; the welcome email appears in the log ~3 s LATER on an [async-N] thread
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Asha Rao",
  "email": "asha@example.com"
}

### 2) Staff email -> the conditional listener (condition = "...endsWith('@course.com')") also fires
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ravi Kumar",
  "email": "ravi@course.com"
}

### 3) Email containing "fail" -> transaction ROLLS BACK -> AFTER_ROLLBACK listener runs, NO welcome email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Broken User",
  "email": "fail@example.com"
}

### 4) List users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### 5) Dashboard: 3 @Async calls in parallel -> timeTakenMs is about 1000, not 3000
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard

### 6) Fire-and-forget @Async job that fails -> 202 at once, error logged by AsyncUncaughtExceptionHandler
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/rebuild-index
